==Mechanics==
===Attack styles===
Skeletal wyverns attack with [[Melee]], [[Ranged]] and their unique ice breath attack.
*The Melee attack is only used when the player is standing in Melee distance and can hit up to 13. Skeletal wyverns roll their slash accuracy against the player's stab defence when performing a bite or tail swipe attack.{{CiteTwitter|author=Mod Ash|url=https://twitter.com/JagexAsh/status/1256193891507847171|date=1 May 2020|archiveurl=https://reldo.runescape.wiki/i/100103|archivedate=5 May 2023|quote=Both the bite and the tail attack are rolling its slash accuracy against your stab defence. The dev didn't leave a comment to say why.}}
*The Ranged attack has an attack range of 6 tiles and can hit up to 13.
*The ice-breath attack has an attack range of 5 tiles and can hit 50+, although this damage can be drastically reduced to a maximum hit of 10 by the following shields: [[elemental shield]], [[mind shield]], [[dragonfire shield]], [[ancient wyvern shield]], and [[dragonfire ward]].
**This attack may also freeze the player's character for a few seconds. During this period, the character is not able to move or attack.
**There is a 1/7 chance to be frozen while wielding one of the shields listed above.{{CiteTwitter|author=Mod Ash|url=https://twitter.com/JagexAsh/status/1247838176753917952|date=8 April 2020|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web20200408104846/https://twitter.com/JagexAsh/status/1247838176753917952|archivedate=8 April 2020|quote=It's doing a 1/7 roll if you have the shield, irrespective of stats.}}
**The [[ancient wyvern shield]] will grant an immunity against this freezing effect.
** Without an appropriate shield, the chance to be frozen by a skeletal wyvern is determined by one's Magic defensive bonuses.{{CiteTwitter|author=Mod Ash|url=https://twitter.com/JagexAsh/status/1247831120777011205|date=8 April 2020|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web20200408101930/https://twitter.com/JagexAsh/status/1247831120777011205|archivedate=8 April 2020|quote=[Does magic level or anything else affect the chance of getting frozen?] It does if you haven't got some protective kit like an appropriate shield.}}
**[[Antifire potion]]s have '''no effect'''.

==Tips==
===Dragonbane weapons===
Because skeletal wyverns are considered to be [[Draconic (attribute)|draconic]] creatures, they are weak against [[dragonbane weapons]]. Therefore it is recommended to use a [[dragon hunter crossbow]] or [[dragon hunter lance]] if any of these weapons are available. They are also one of the few draconic creatures that are affected by the enchanted dragonstone bolt effect, ''Dragon's breath''.

===Safespotting===

Skeletal wyverns can be safespotted because they have a shorter attack range than players using a crossbow or magic spells. They can be easily safespotted during a Slayer task by standing one tile north-west of [[Steve]]/[[Pieve]]. 

#To safespot skeletal wyverns, first make sure to lose their [[aggressiveness]]. Aggressiveness is lost automatically after a player has spent 10 minutes in the same area (i.e. they don't move past a certain invisible border).
#After this time period, attack a wyvern and lure it behind an obstacle (e.g. a wall that is sticking out).
#While the wyvern is stuck behind the obstacle, move out of its attack range to make sure it can't attack the player anymore.
#Now start attacking the wyvern using [[Magic]] or [[Ranged]].

Another common method for doing this is getting them stuck behind the main entrance. Players should always wait for the wyverns to become [[unaggressive]], which takes 10 minutes, before attempting this; otherwise, they'll get hit by other wyverns when trying to safespot another. A good method to make them unaggressive is to wait in front of the main entrance for ten minutes; this will make the wyverns unaggressive near the entrance. Players who do this should be careful not to walk more than a few steps deeper into the cave, as if they do, the wyverns will get [[aggressive]] again. Alternatively, for safespotting, players can bring a few [[Prayer potion]]s and attack the wyvern from seven steps away with [[Protect from Range|Protect from Missiles]] on.

<gallery>
File:Skeletal Wyvern door safespot.png|thumb|300px|The most popular way of [[safespot]]ting Wyverns is done by trapping the eastern or western one on the side of the cave entrance after losing [[aggression]], as shown.
File:Skeletal Wyvern (upper level) safespot.png|thumb|297x297px|Safespot for task-only area.
File:Skeletal Wyvern southern safespot.png|thumb|300px|South of the cave door are some additional [[safespot]]s in which the western and southern sides of the ice structure (or pillar) can be used as safespots.
</gallery>

===Dwarf multicannon===
[[Dwarf multicannon]] are allowed in the [[Asgarnian Ice Dungeon]], however only in the lower part of the cave; the upper Slayer-exclusive part is a no cannon zone. Cannons will make killing skeletal wyverns faster and the profit from the extra drops often outweigh the cost of the [[steel cannonball]]s. Therefore it can be recommended to bring a dwarf multicannon when meleeing skeletal wyverns.

=== Prayers ===
If in melee range then [[Protect from Melee]]; else if ranged/magic and not safespotting then [[Protect from Range]].

