This gear assumes the player uses the safespot method to attack the skeletal wyverns. Wyverns will be aggressive and un-safespottable for the first 10 minutes, so it's necessary to bring an icy breath protection shield. Once they become [[tolerant]], players should switch to their [[tome of fire]]. Wyverns can be lured incorrectly, which allows them to use their icy breath attack, so keep the protective shield in the inventory.

This is the best-in-slot available equipment for maging skeletal wyverns. The set up shown in this section currently costs approximately {{Coins|{{GEP|Ancestral hat}} + {{GEP|Occult necklace}} + {{GEP|Dragon hunter wand}} + {{GEP|Ancestral robe top}} + {{GEP|Ancestral robe bottom}} + {{GEP|Tome of Fire (empty)}} + {{GEP|Confliction gauntlets}} + {{GEP|Eternal boots}} + {{GEP|Avernic treads}} + {{GEP|Demon tear}}*4000 + {{GEP|Magus ring}} + {{GEP|Imbued heart}}}} coins. See the table below for an overview of equipment alternatives in case this setup is not accessible or too expensive.

===Notes===
*Casting [[fire spells]] with a charged [[tome of fire]] equipped or [[water spells]] with a charged [[tome of water]] equipped will increase the spell's damage by 10%.
*The  [[confliction gauntlets]] (+7%), [[occult necklace]] (+5%), [[tormented bracelet]] (+5%), [[imbued god capes]] (+2%), [[magus ring]] (+2%), and [[seers ring]] (0.5%) increase the maximum hit of the player's Magic spells.
* [[Ancestral robes]] (+3% each) and [[Virtus robes]] (+2% each) [+5% each using the Ancient spell book] increases the maximum hit of the player's Magic spells.

